think The next doors named were line_project (each object's foot on the line) and line_band (a corridor marquee within a distance threshold). Chose line_band Lindy-first crux-first: it is a durable, reusable SELECTION gesture (a lasso along a stroke) and it stays fully exact-integer, where line_project's foot needs a rational point that would depart the family's no-divide/no-sqrt discipline.
think The decisive crux: a corridor is a SUBLEVEL SET of the sorted distance key, so line_band is a PREFIX of line_distance's nearest-to-farthest order. The exact-integer test is key*key <= 4*half_width^2*len2 (squaring clears the root over doubled coordinates), so the boundary is sharp and closed, the band nests monotonically, and it is blind to the drawn direction where line_partition's sides swap.
think Composed over line_distance's public reads (distance_of, line_distance, on_line), line_partition's object_side (the direction-blind cross-check), and click_collinear's click_group_center_doubled (the squared length) -- no plane of its own, a reading over readings.
obs Built over line_distance's own six-object 20x14 scene so the corridor is read over the same picture the triad closed on: distances A0 B0 P3 Q3 D4 U5, so half-width 3 selects exactly {A,B,P,Q}, P at distance exactly 3 held at width 3 and dropped at width 2 (the boundary proven by an object standing on it), band_count nondecreasing 2/4/5/6 across widths 0/3/4/5, width 0 collapsing to the on_line set, the reversed line selecting the identical corridor.
